diff --git a/docs/api.rst b/docs/api.rst
index b2db5375..af4e97a9 100644
--- a/docs/api.rst
+++ b/docs/api.rst
@@ -443,6 +443,22 @@ own loader, subclass :class:`BaseLoader` and override `get_source`.
 Here a list of the builtin loaders Jinja provides:
 
 .. autoclass:: jinja2.FileSystemLoader
+    :members: start_monitoring, scan_once, invalidate_changed, close
+
+Filesystem loaders can proactively invalidate template caches. The
+``auto_reload`` loader option defaults to true and starts polling at
+0.5-second intervals when an Environment first requests a source. It is
+independent of the Environment's lazy ``auto_reload`` freshness checks.
+Environments are tracked weakly; disabled loader monitoring does not
+register them or start a thread. Filesystem errors do not end polling.
+
+``scan_once`` compares snapshots synchronously. ``invalidate_changed``
+accepts absolute paths, ignores paths outside the roots, and returns
+canonical template names using ``/``. Unrelated cached names and other
+loaders remain untouched; an Environment without a cache is supported.
+Call ``close`` to stop polling, or use the loader as a context manager.
+Repeated lifecycle calls are safe and an explicit start can restart a
+closed monitor. Relative source paths retain their lookup rules.
 
 .. autoclass:: jinja2.PackageLoader
 
@@ -920,3 +936,5 @@ returned by the :meth:`Environment.parse` method.
 .. autofunction:: jinja2.meta.find_undeclared_variables
 
 .. autofunction:: jinja2.meta.find_referenced_templates
+
+Closing permanently disables the loader; monitoring replaces all lazy freshness checks.
